{% comment %}
  Beyond Beyond skincare assistant.

  The widget's job is to turn a conversation into a routine the visitor can buy without ever
  leaving it: the assistant recommends products, they add them inline, and the routine tray
  above the composer keeps a running count and total with a checkout button. Nothing here
  sends the visitor to another page until they choose to check out.

  Include once, near the end of theme.liquid, before </body>:
    {% render 'beyond-chatbot' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  comment
    The header carries the logo, not a wordmark. It defaults to the same file the site header
    uses, and a merchant can point it at a different one -- a tall or stacked lockup often
    wants a more compact variant at this size. Falls back to the brand logo, then to the shop
    name, so the header is never empty.
  endcomment
  assign chat_logo = settings.chat_logo | default: shop.brand.logo
  assign chat_logo_height = settings.chat_logo_height | default: 34
  assign chat_logo_height_2x = chat_logo_height | times: 2

  comment
    The handoff only exists if there is somewhere to hand off to. Each channel is
    independent, so a merchant with only WhatsApp gets a one-row sheet rather than an
    empty shell with a heading.
  endcomment
  assign whatsapp = settings.chat_whatsapp | strip | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-'
  assign phone = settings.chat_phone | strip
  assign booking = settings.chat_booking_url
  assign chat_email = settings.chat_email | strip

  assign has_human = false
  if settings.chat_human_enabled
    if whatsapp != blank or phone != blank or booking != blank or chat_email != blank
      assign has_human = true
    endif
  endif
-%}

{{ 'beyond-chatbot.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<div
  class="bb-chat"
  data-bb-root
  data-bb-hours-days="{{ settings.chat_human_days | default: 'mon-sat' }}"
  data-bb-hours-open="{{ settings.chat_human_open | default: 10 }}"
  data-bb-hours-close="{{ settings.chat_human_close | default: 19 }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Sits behind the panel and blurs everything behind it -- the rest of the
    page, not the widget itself, since the panel and launcher are stacked
    above it. Clicking it closes the panel, the same as clicking outside any
    other dialog.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div id="bb-backdrop" class="bb-backdrop" data-bb-backdrop aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <button
    id="bb-launcher"
    class="bb-launcher"
    type="button"
    aria-label="Open the skincare assistant"
    aria-expanded="false"
    aria-controls="bb-panel"
  >
    <span class="bb-launcher__mark" aria-hidden="true">
      <img
        src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0715/1157/2666/files/Group_1180.png?v=1788421980"
        alt=""
        width="61"
        height="39"
        loading="lazy"
      >
    </span>
    <span class="bb-launcher__pip" data-bb-pip hidden></span>
  </button>

  <section
    id="bb-panel"
    class="bb-panel"
    role="dialog"
    aria-label="Beyond Beyond skincare assistant"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
    <header class="bb-header">
      <div class="bb-header__brand">
        {% comment %} {%- if chat_logo != blank -%}
          <img
            class="bb-header__logo"
            srcset="{{ chat_logo | image_url: height: chat_logo_height }} 1x, {{ chat_logo | image_url: height: chat_logo_height_2x }} 2x"
            src="{{ chat_logo | image_url: height: chat_logo_height }}"
            alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
            {%- comment -%}
              The store's logos are SVGs, and Shopify reports no intrinsic width or aspect
              ratio for those -- deriving width from aspect_ratio would render width="0" and
              collapse the logo. The site header has the same problem and omits width, so the
              browser takes it from the SVG. Only raster logos get an explicit width.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if chat_logo.aspect_ratio > 0 %}
              width="{{ chat_logo_height | times: chat_logo.aspect_ratio | ceil }}"
            {% endif -%}
            height="{{ chat_logo_height }}"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        {%- else -%}
          <span class="bb-header__wordmark">{{ shop.name }}</span>
        {%- endif -%} {% endcomment %}
        <span class="bb-header__role">Skincare assistant</span>
      </div>

      <div class="bb-header__actions">
        {%- if has_human -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            An icon rather than a labelled pill: at this panel width a text button would
            have to push the brand lockup out to fit, and the whole point of the handoff is
            that it waits quietly until it is wanted. The transcript surfaces a labelled
            prompt at the moment someone actually needs a person -- see bb-nudge.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button
            id="bb-human"
            class="bb-iconbtn bb-iconbtn--human"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Talk to a human"
            title="Talk to a human"
            aria-haspopup="dialog"
          >
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M4 13v-1a8 8 0 0 1 16 0v1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              <path d="M4 13h1.6a1.4 1.4 0 0 1 1.4 1.4v3.2A1.4 1.4 0 0 1 5.6 19H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1v-5ZM20 13h-1.6a1.4 1.4 0 0 0-1.4 1.4v3.2a1.4 1.4 0 0 0 1.4 1.4h.6a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-5Z" fill="currentColor"/>
            </svg>
            <span class="bb-iconbtn__dot" data-bb-live-dot aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
        {%- endif -%}

        <button id="bb-reset" class="bb-iconbtn" type="button" aria-label="Start a new conversation">
          {{- 'icon-bb-reset.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
        </button>
        <button id="bb-close" class="bb-iconbtn" type="button" aria-label="Close chat">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div id="bb-body" class="bb-body" role="log" aria-live="polite" aria-relevant="additions">
      <div id="bb-welcome" class="bb-welcome">
        <p class="bb-welcome__lead">
          Tell me about your skin and I'll build you a routine — and you can add every step to
          your bag right here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      The routine tray. Stays hidden until something is in the bag, then docks above the
      composer with a running total so the routine is always visible as it is assembled.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div id="bb-tray" class="bb-tray" hidden>
      <button
        id="bb-tray-toggle"
        class="bb-tray__handle"
        type="button"
        aria-expanded="false"
        aria-controls="bb-tray-drawer"
      >
        <span class="bb-tray__stack" data-bb-tray-stack aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="bb-tray__meta">
          <span class="bb-tray__label">Your routine</span>
          <span class="bb-tray__count" data-bb-tray-count></span>
        </span>
        <span class="bb-tray__total" data-bb-tray-total></span>
        <svg class="bb-tray__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M7 14l5-5 5 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
      </button>

      <div id="bb-tray-drawer" class="bb-tray__drawer">
        <ul class="bb-tray__list" data-bb-tray-list></ul>
        <a class="bb-tray__checkout" href="{{ routes.root_url }}checkout">
          <span>Checkout</span>
          <span class="bb-tray__checkout-total" data-bb-tray-total></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="bb-chips" class="bb-chips"></div>

    <div class="bb-composer">
      <div id="bb-suggest" class="bb-suggest" role="listbox" aria-label="Suggested questions" hidden></div>

      {%- comment -%}
        The attached photo, shown as a chip above the row rather than inside the field --
        the field's ghost-completion layer mirrors the input's box exactly, and anything
        placed inside it would have to be mirrored there too.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if settings.chat_photo_enabled -%}
        <div class="bb-attach" data-bb-attach hidden>
          <img class="bb-attach__thumb" data-bb-attach-thumb alt="" width="40" height="40">
          <span class="bb-attach__meta">
            <span class="bb-attach__title">Photo attached</span>
            <span class="bb-attach__note" data-bb-attach-note>Analysed once. Never stored.</span>
          </span>
          <button class="bb-attach__remove" type="button" data-bb-attach-remove aria-label="Remove photo">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="bb-composer__row">
        {%- if settings.chat_photo_enabled -%}
          <button id="bb-photo" class="bb-photo" type="button" aria-label="Add a photo of your skin">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M4 8.5h2.6l1.2-2h8.4l1.2 2H20a1 1 0 0 1 1 1V18a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V9.5a1 1 0 0 1 1-1Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              <circle cx="12" cy="13.2" r="3.1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/>
            </svg>
          </button>
          <input
            id="bb-photo-input"
            class="bb-visually-hidden"
            type="file"
            accept="image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp"
            tabindex="-1"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="bb-field">
          {%- comment -%}
            Ghost layer sits behind the input and mirrors its metrics exactly, so the greyed
            completion lines up with what has already been typed. bb-ghost__typed is invisible
            and only there to push the completion to the right offset.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="bb-ghost" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="bb-ghost__typed" data-bb-ghost-typed></span><span class="bb-ghost__rest" data-bb-ghost-rest></span>
          </div>
          <input
            id="bb-input"
            class="bb-input"
            type="text"
            placeholder="Ask about your skin…"
            autocomplete="off"
            autocapitalize="sentences"
            spellcheck="false"
            role="combobox"
            aria-autocomplete="both"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="bb-suggest"
          />
        </div>

        <button id="bb-send" class="bb-send" type="button" aria-label="Send message">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 12l16-7-6 7 6 7-16-7z" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>

      <p class="bb-composer__hint" data-bb-hint hidden>
        Press <kbd>Tab</kbd> to complete
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Sheets. Both slide up inside the panel over a scrim rather than opening a dialog of
      their own -- the visitor never loses the conversation they were having, and coming
      back is a dismiss rather than a navigation.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if has_human -%}
      <div class="bb-scrim" data-bb-scrim hidden></div>

      <div
        id="bb-human-sheet"
        class="bb-sheet"
        role="dialog"
        aria-label="Talk to a human"
        aria-modal="true"
        hidden
      >
        <button class="bb-sheet__close" type="button" data-bb-sheet-close aria-label="Close">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <p class="bb-sheet__title">Talk to a human</p>
        <p class="bb-sheet__status" data-bb-status>
          <span class="bb-sheet__dot" data-bb-live-dot aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span data-bb-status-text>{{ settings.chat_human_hours }}</span>
        </p>

        <div class="bb-channels">
          {%- if whatsapp != blank -%}
            <a class="bb-channel" href="https://wa.me/{{ whatsapp }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="bb-channel__icon bb-channel__icon--whatsapp" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <path d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 0-7.7 13.7L3 21l4.4-1.2A9 9 0 1 0 12 3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                  <path d="M9.2 8.2c.3-.1.6 0 .8.3l.7 1.2c.1.3.1.6-.1.8l-.4.5c-.1.2-.2.4 0 .6.5.8 1.1 1.4 1.9 1.9.2.1.4.1.6-.1l.5-.4c.2-.2.5-.2.8-.1l1.2.7c.3.2.4.5.3.8-.2.7-.9 1.2-1.7 1.2-2.4 0-5.4-3-5.4-5.4 0-.8.5-1.5 1.2-1.7l-.4-.3Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="bb-channel__text">
                <span class="bb-channel__label">WhatsApp</span>
                <span class="bb-channel__note">Usually replies in minutes</span>
              </span>
              <svg class="bb-channel__go" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if booking != blank -%}
            <a class="bb-channel" href="{{ booking }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="bb-channel__icon bb-channel__icon--book" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <rect x="3.5" y="5.5" width="17" height="15" rx="2.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/>
                  <path d="M3.5 10h17M8.5 3.5v4M15.5 3.5v4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="bb-channel__text">
                <span class="bb-channel__label">Book a consultation</span>
                <span class="bb-channel__note">
                  {{- settings.chat_booking_note | default: 'Pick a time that suits you' -}}
                </span>
              </span>
              <svg class="bb-channel__go" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if phone != blank -%}
            <a class="bb-channel" href="tel:{{ phone | remove: ' ' }}">
              <span class="bb-channel__icon bb-channel__icon--call" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <path d="M6.6 4h2.5l1.4 3.5-1.8 1.3a10.5 10.5 0 0 0 4.5 4.5l1.3-1.8L18 12.9v2.5c0 1-.8 1.8-1.8 1.7A13.4 13.4 0 0 1 4.9 5.8 1.7 1.7 0 0 1 6.6 4Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="bb-channel__text">
                <span class="bb-channel__label">Call us</span>
                <span class="bb-channel__note">{{ phone }}</span>
              </span>
              <svg class="bb-channel__go" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if chat_email != blank -%}
            <a class="bb-channel" href="mailto:{{ chat_email }}">
              <span class="bb-channel__icon bb-channel__icon--mail" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <rect x="3.5" y="5.5" width="17" height="13" rx="2.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7"/>
                  <path d="M4.5 7.5l7.5 5.5 7.5-5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
              <span class="bb-channel__text">
                <span class="bb-channel__label">Email</span>
                <span class="bb-channel__note">{{ chat_email }}</span>
              </span>
              <svg class="bb-channel__go" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <p class="bb-sheet__foot">Or keep chatting here — I'll be right where you left off.</p>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if settings.chat_photo_enabled -%}
      {%- unless has_human -%}
        <div class="bb-scrim" data-bb-scrim hidden></div>
      {%- endunless -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Shown once, before the first photo is ever chosen. A face is not an ordinary
        attachment, so what happens to it is said plainly before the picker opens rather
        than in fine print underneath it afterwards.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div
        id="bb-photo-sheet"
        class="bb-sheet"
        role="dialog"
        aria-label="Add a photo of your skin"
        aria-modal="true"
        hidden
      >
        <button class="bb-sheet__close" type="button" data-bb-sheet-close aria-label="Close">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6L6 18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <p class="bb-sheet__title">Show me your skin</p>
        <p class="bb-sheet__lead">
          A clear, well-lit photo of your bare face lets me tailor the routine to what I can
          actually see — texture, tone, shine, dryness.
        </p>

        <ul class="bb-facts">
          <li class="bb-fact">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 3.5l7 3v5.2c0 4.1-2.9 7.4-7 8.8-4.1-1.4-7-4.7-7-8.8V6.5l7-3Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              <path d="M9 12l2.2 2.2L15.5 10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
            <span>Analysed once, then discarded. It is never stored or shown to anyone.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="bb-fact">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/>
              <path d="M12 11v5.5M12 7.8v.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
            <span>Cosmetic guidance, not a medical diagnosis. See a dermatologist for that.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <button class="bb-sheet__cta" type="button" data-bb-photo-continue>Choose a photo</button>
        <button class="bb-sheet__ghost" type="button" data-bb-sheet-close>Not now</button>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  GSAP drives the panel choreography, the message and product staggers, and the add-to-routine
  flight. This theme already loads gsap.min.js once, site-wide, in theme.liquid -- a second copy
  here would start a second ticker and fight the first for window.gsap -- so only the widget's
  own script is included. beyond-chatbot.js still checks for window.gsap and falls back to CSS
  transitions if it is ever missing.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'beyond-chatbot.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
